WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.626
Hi! Adjectives and adverbs are both describing words, but they describe different things. Today we'll learn to tell them apart, and also learn comparing words and word forms.

2
00:00:13.776 --> 00:00:20.466
An adjective describes a person or thing. In a careful driver, careful describes the driver.

3
00:00:20.616 --> 00:00:27.498
An adverb tells us how an action is done. In he drives carefully, carefully describes drives.

4
00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:38.802
Many adverbs are adjectives plus l-y: quick becomes quickly. If it ends in y, change y to i: happy becomes happily. Gentle becomes gently.

5
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:48.690
Some are special: the adverb of good is well, and fast and hard stay the same. She runs fast. He works hard.

6
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:56.874
Compare two with e-r, and three or more with e-s-t. Ali is taller than Ben. Sam is the tallest in the class.

7
00:00:57.024 --> 00:01:02.298
Big doubles the g: bigger. Heavy changes y to i: heavier.

8
00:01:02.448 --> 00:01:07.410
Long words use more and most: more beautiful, the most beautiful.

9
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:14.682
Some are irregular: good, better, best, and bad, worse, worst.

10
00:01:14.832 --> 00:01:21.930
One word can change its form. Kind is an adjective, kindness is a noun, and kindly is an adverb.

11
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:32.562
Look around the ___. After the or a we need a noun. After a verb we often need an adverb. Before a noun we need an adjective.

12
00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:36.762
Watch out! She sings beautiful is wrong!

13
00:01:36.912 --> 00:01:41.922
The word describes the action, sings, so we need the adverb beautifully.

14
00:01:42.072 --> 00:01:48.642
But for the song itself, we say a beautiful song, with an adjective for the noun.

15
00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:58.962
Your turn! The baby slept, ___. Use the right form of peaceful. Pause and think.

16
00:01:59.112 --> 00:02:07.122
Peacefully. It describes how the baby slept, so we need an adverb. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:07.272 --> 00:02:17.754
Another one! This box is, ___, than that one. Use the right form of heavy. Pause and think.

18
00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:26.274
Heavier. Than means we compare two things, so change y to i and add e-r. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:26.424 --> 00:02:36.882
Next one! Mei plays the piano very, ___. Use the right form of good. Pause and think.

20
00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:46.170
Well. It describes how she plays, so we need an adverb, and the adverb of good is well. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:56.106
Last one! Thank you for your, ___. Use the right form of kind. Pause and think.

22
00:02:56.256 --> 00:03:02.610
Kindness. After your, we need a noun. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:11.946
Remember: adjectives describe nouns, adverbs describe actions. Many adverbs end in l-y, and the adverb of good is well.

24
00:03:12.096 --> 00:03:21.258
Use e-r or more for two, and e-s-t or most for three or more. For word forms, look around the ___ to see what kind of word is needed.

25
00:03:21.408 --> 00:03:26.754
Today, use three adverbs to tell how you do things!

